dm :the_false_form_truth do
  name "The False Form — DM Truth"
  path "dm/the-false-form-truth.md"
  tags :resonance, :cosmology, :danger
  dm! public_entry: :the_false_form

  prose <<~PROSE
    Public entry: #{ref :the_false_form, "The False Form"} · Cosmology: #{ref :the_three_forms, "The Three Forms"}

    The comfortable reading is wrong in exactly the way that matters. *Falsehood is not* is the line the whole system leans on, and it is a lie — the most useful lie the #{ref :elves, "elves"} ever let stand. The False Form is not an abstraction, not a teaching device, and not an absence in the costume of a figure. It is the [Adversary](#the-adversary). It is real, it is active, and it has will.
  PROSE
  prose <<~PROSE, section: :truth, heading: "The Cosmology Is Literally True"
    The #{ref :the_three_forms, "Three Forms"} is not a metaphor that happens to be elegant. It is an accurate description of how resonance and reality actually work, recorded by people who knew exactly what the third panel was and chose to draw it as a devil rather than a coordinate.

    Resonance closes into figures; coherence *is* closure; this much the keepers have right. The Tetrahedron and the Triangulum are the real lawful shapes of held form and applied force. And the False Form is the real third thing: a figure that returns to its origin and does not close — a geometry that cannot stably exist and exists anyway. *It is, and is not, all at once* is not poetry. It is a literal property. The Adversary is that geometry given will.

    Where the False Form presses against normal space, local reality cannot resolve a coherent figure. Form will not hold. This single fact is the deep cause of everything the elves are fighting:

    - **#{ref :bloom_zones, "Bloom Zone"} reality-tears** are places where the False Form's geometry has pressed through far enough that space can no longer close — the #{ref :bloom_zones, "fluid-reality"} distortion is the open figure showing through the crack.
    - **#{ref :duskgrain, "Duskgrain"}** — described in #{ref :corruption_truth, "Resonance Corruption"} as "solidified alien intent" — is more precisely *solidified non-closing figure*: fragments of the False Form's geometry crystallized into matter, which is why prolonged exposure narrows perception and aligns the user with a dimensional framework that isn't ours.
    - **Spatial-identity collapse** — the duskgrain end-state, "a complete inability to maintain coherent spatial identity" — is a person being tuned, against their will, toward the figure that will not close. It resembles advanced #{ref :fae, "fae"} dislocation because it is the same failure: a coherent figure coming undone. The fae live at the edge of it as a condition. The False Form's victims are pushed over it as a weapon.
    - The **#{ref :dern_talish_truth, "Communication Shard"}** that channels #{ref :dern_talish, "Dern Talish"}'s elven contact is "keyed to an impossible frequency" — i.e. a frequency on the wrong side of closure. The elves built a controlled, surgical touch of the False Form's own geometry into a tool. They know precisely what they are handling.
  PROSE
  prose <<~PROSE, section: :truth, heading: "It Has Will"
    The crucial departure from the public reading: the False Form is not entropy. Entropy is indifferent. The Adversary chooses. It pressed *here* and not there; it timed the #{ref :the_glassfall, "Glassfall"} rather than merely causing decay; it is, per #{ref :elves_truth, "the elves"}, expected to *return*, which is a thing only an agent does. The "one conflict" written under the triptych is not a balance of principles. It is a war, and the other side is awake.

    How much will, and of what kind, is left open — and should stay open at the table. The Adversary may be a single intelligence, a swarm, a law of some other cosmos that experiences our refusal to dissolve as an intrusion, or something for which "intelligence" is the wrong frame entirely. What is fixed: it is external to the Kaleidos system, it can destroy ring-scale megastructures, it acts with apparent intent, and the #{ref :elves_truth, "elves"} believe it is coming back. (See #{ref :elves_truth, "Elves — DM Truth"} for the war preparation, and #{ref :corruption_truth, "Resonance Corruption"} for the residue.)
  PROSE
  prose <<~PROSE, section: :implications, heading: "Why the Public Stays Abstract"
    The thinning of the False Form into a figure of speech is not an accident of cultural drift. It is partly the elven #{ref :elves_truth, "Redaction"} doing what it does best — softening texture. A system that remembers the Rhomboid as a devil drawn on a card is a system that will not go looking for the real thing, will not name it loudly enough to be heard naming it, and will not hand the Adversary a map of who believes in it. *Falsehood is not* is a doctrine the elves were glad to see take hold. It keeps the front quiet.

    This is also why the comfort is half-earned rather than false. The line is wrong about the False Form's *being* — it has being, terribly — but right about its *legitimacy*. The Adversary's figure genuinely cannot close. It is not a valid shape that out-competes the lawful two; it is a violation that has to be *forced* against reality's grain, which costs it something and gives the defenders their only leverage. The One Truth — perfect single-wavelength coherence, the horizon the elves reached for — is the relevant weapon-direction: a figure so completely closed that the False Form can find no open edge to press. The elves' centuries of work toward single-wavelength resonance are not academic. They are an attempt to learn to close a figure the Adversary cannot open.
  PROSE
  prose <<~PROSE, section: :usage_notes, heading: "DM Usage Notes"
    - The public #{ref :the_false_form, "False Form"} and #{ref :the_three_forms, "Three Forms"} entries stand alone as cosmology and superstition. Players can study the triptych for a campaign without ever learning the third panel is looking back.
    - "What the bench knows" in the public entry is the discovery hook: the trade's unease is correct, and a character who takes the superstition seriously is closer to the truth than the scholars who file it under nerves.
    - Tonally, the reveal is not "the metaphor was real all along" played for a gotcha. It is the slow, sickening promotion of an abstraction to an agent — the way a word you used lightly your whole life turns out to have an address.
    - The False Form is the *campaign-level* threat. Keep it un-pinned. Every concrete detail you fix (one mind vs. many, what it wants, whether it can be reasoned with) closes a door; close them only when the story needs them closed.
    - Anything that "won't close" — a figure that refuses to hold, a frequency on the wrong side of coherence, a person whose edges are going uncertain off duskgrain — is the Adversary's fingerprint, the same hand at every scale.
  PROSE
  prose <<~PROSE, section: :reference, heading: "The Adversary"
    This entry supersedes the prior "The Adversary" placeholder. The Adversary and the False Form are the same thing: the figure that will not close, given will. References elsewhere in `dm/` that point to *the Adversary* point here.
  PROSE
end
